  q(CARE,'Which finding should be reported after measuring a resident’s blood pressure?','A reading of 168/104 mmHg',['A reading of 118/76 mmHg','A reading of 112/72 mmHg','A reading of 120/78 mmHg'],'D','A reading this high is in the hypertension range and needs quick follow-up by the nurse.',DUG),
  q(CARE,'What is the correct way to apply anti-embolism stockings?','Before the resident gets out of bed',['After the resident walks for an hour','While the resident stands in the shower','Only when the legs are very swollen'],'A','Applying them while lying down keeps blood from pooling in the legs.',DUG),
  q(CARE,'What is the purpose of a bed cradle?','Keep linens off the feet and legs',['Raise the bed to working height','Hold urine drainage bags','Store residents’ personal items'],'B','A bed cradle prevents pressure from sheets on sore or injured legs.',DUG),
  q(DIS,'Which action helps a resident who is constipated?','Encourage fluids, fiber and activity',['Limit all water and juice','Keep the resident in bed all day','Remove fruit from all meals'],'C','Report constipation to the nurse, who may order other treatments.',DUG),
  q(CARE,'What is the correct way to measure a resident’s radial pulse?','Use two fingers for 30 or 60 seconds',['Use the thumb for 5 seconds','Press hard with the palm','Count only while the resident talks'],'D','The thumb has its own pulse and can lead to an inaccurate count.',DUG),
  q(CARE,'How should a nursing assistant help a resident use a bedpan?','Raise the head of the bed if allowed',['Leave the resident flat on the back','Put the bedpan in place without warning','Leave the call light out of reach'],'A','Sitting up makes it easier for the resident to have a bowel movement.',DUG),
  q(CARE,'Which observation should be reported for a resident with a feeding tube?','Coughing or trouble breathing',['Clean, dry skin at the site','Resting quietly in bed','A good mood during care'],'B','Coughing or trouble breathing may mean formula has entered the lungs (aspiration).',DUG),
  q(CARE,'How should a nursing assistant clean a resident’s eyeglasses?','With water and a soft cloth',['With paper towels and bleach','With a rough washcloth only','With hot water and sandpaper'],'C','Use water or lens cleaner and a soft cloth, since paper towels can scratch the lenses.',DUG),
  q(CARE,'Which action is correct when caring for a resident’s fingernails?','Clean under nails with an orange stick',['Cut nails with sharp scissors','Cut diabetic residents’ toenails','Trim nails while the resident sleeps'],'D','Nail care for diabetic residents is done by a nurse or podiatrist.',DUG),
  q(CARE,'Which observation after a meal should be reported?','The resident ate less than half',['The resident ate all the food','The resident drank milk and juice','The resident asked for dessert'],'A','A drop in appetite may signal illness and can quickly affect a resident’s nutrition.',DUG),
  q(DIS,'Which condition causes painful, swollen joints from cartilage wearing away over time?','Osteoarthritis',['Diabetes mellitus','Angina pectoris','Hepatitis B'],'B','Gentle exercise, warm baths and rest periods can ease osteoarthritis pain and stiffness.',DUG),
  q(DIS,'Which sign is common in a resident with hypoglycemia?','Cold, clammy skin',['Fruity breath odor','Dry, flushed skin','Deep, rapid breathing'],'C','Low blood sugar triggers cold, clammy skin, sweating, shakiness and confusion.',DUG),
  q(DIS,'Which condition is a progressive loss of muscle control caused by nerve cell death?','Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis',['Seasonal allergic rhinitis','Common cold virus','Mild sunburn on the skin'],'D','ALS affects voluntary muscles, including those used to swallow and breathe.',DUG),
  q(DIS,'Which care is most important for a resident with a seizure disorder?','Protect the head and do not restrain',['Hold the resident’s arms tightly','Put a spoon in the resident’s mouth','Give water during the seizure'],'A','Move objects away, note how long the seizure lasts and report it to the nurse.',DUG),
  q(DIS,'Which problem is common after a stroke affecting the face and throat?','Dysphagia (trouble swallowing)',['Better taste and smell','Faster speech than normal','Extra saliva production only'],'B','Thickened liquids, small bites and upright positioning may be ordered to prevent choking.',DUG),
  q(DIS,'Which condition causes airways to narrow and wheeze, often triggered by allergens?','Asthma',['Gout','Anemia','Cataracts'],'C','Rescue inhalers open the narrowed airways during an asthma attack.',DUG),
  q(DIS,'Which is a common sign of depression in an older adult?','Loss of interest in activities',['More social activity','A greater appetite at meals','Better sleep habits at night'],'D','Depression is treatable and is not a normal part of aging, so changes should be reported.',DUG),
  q(DIS,'Which condition involves too much sugar in the blood due to insulin problems?','Diabetes mellitus',['Hypothyroidism','Osteoporosis','Emphysema'],'A','Diet, exercise and medications help keep blood sugar in a healthy range.',DUG),
  q(DIS,'Which finding is common in a resident with cataracts?','Cloudy or blurry vision',['Pain in the ear canal','Ringing in both ears','Loss of taste for food'],'B','Cataracts cloud the lens of the eye and can be removed with surgery.',DUG)
